 " that has one and preserves the order of the ticks.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"5bbc6e69-d485-4c77-88b6-024b51cd2e63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Statement: with ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "\:207a(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \:2229 ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " the message relation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "813fdb3d-2360-4be6-afc1-f00aeea0bef1"],
 ", an association ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " is a message function from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " when"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"44b1146c-cfc4-41e6-82ef-0b970852aecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "its keys are exactly the ticks ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[NotEqual] \[EmptySet],"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"157c8ade-0a94-452f-ba16-d80206dcb301"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") for every key, and"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d0496e7f-ae76-49a7-9065-a5ba14fde43f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the positions of ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") on ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " do not decrease as ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " runs along ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4839aa7d-3ac3-404f-994a-54bc5ff20666"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the discrete form of the EPS axiom D1: a message function is \
single-valued on its domain and order-preserving. The order of the keys in ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " does not matter. A partial map, a map to a tick off the light cone and a \
multivalued map fail. The predicate tests a candidate map against the pair of \
observers; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["EPSMessageAxiomQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/EPSMessageAxiomQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9ba06ac2-f872-4eae-a301-c193ed557852"],
 " tests the pair itself, whether the relation is already such a map on every \
tick."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2ebc5691-d562-4eab-85cb-178c7f416821"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMemberQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMemberQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b7d8311a-d01f-491e-b86d-43033fa7225a"],
 " on the head is this predicate, and the members drawn by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/RandomInfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "61c0e1fe-c81b-4fb5-a1ee-5b081ab24299"],
 " all pass. When no tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " reaches ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", the empty association is the one message function."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5fc030fd-cc3b-410e-b7d4-ef9b0fbdf953"],

Cell["\<\
The three conditions are independent: the order condition can fail with every \
image admissible, when the images of two ticks are chosen crosswise.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"94c0d8fd-661e-47b9-8f36-51686bcb65e6"]
}, Open  ]],

